      "mergeID": "668d806555183ae21d70d2f3",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Today, every time I tried to load into a world, it's taking 60 seconds on the \"Connecting\" screen. I checked the logs and it's always saying it's \"Waiting for network limits\" during that time.\n\nBeing 60 seconds every time makes me feel like I'm hitting a timeout of some sort. Does anyone know why?\n\nI've tried reinstalling VRChat.\n\n2024.07.02 22:59:21 Log        -  [Behaviour] Waiting for network limits.\n\n2024.07.02 23:00:21 Log        -  [Behaviour] Spent 60.65991s waiting for network limits.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "\"Waiting for network limits\" almost exactly 60 seconds?",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "668792db4ee599a77c74ebf9",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Is this the default home world? Have you tried changing your home world or launching into another world from the VRChat website off of the browser\n\nHave you tried turning off IPV6 on either your computer or router?\n\nHave you also tried using a VPN and then connecting to VRChat?\n\nI recommend also making sure that your PC meets the minimum specs for VRChat and that your PC isn't treating VRChat like a background task\n\nCheck also that your wifi/internet is strong enough to play VRChat with an online speed test \n\nAnd I recommend plugging into ethernet to get a more stable connection\n\nI hope you get more help with this as I'm no expert but I hear those are things that help!\n\nGood luck!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
