      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hey there. I've had this issue for several months now, found out how to fix it for me, posted about it in a different bug report (https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/connection-timed-out-or-vrchat-stopped-responding-error-too-often), so I'll copy my response here as well:\n\n\"After investigating and trying different things to mitigate the issue I've successfully stopped the random timeouts occurring during VRChat sessions.\n\nThe issue seems to be related to ISP's switching to CGNAT instead of using Real Dynamic IP address allocation. This is what happened to me, and my ISP was beginning to assign IP addresses from 10.0.0.0/8 range to me.\n\nHow did I came up with the fix?\n\nAt certain point when going on with my stuff I set up a Plex server at home, but it complained that It wasn't available through the internet (example picture provided), so for some time it had to rely on somewhat bandwidth limited Plex relay servers for streaming media via internet.\n\nSometime after that I learned that my ISP provides a service where for a small monthly fee (0.84€) I could get a Real Dynamic IPv4 WAN address allocation back, so I subscribed and now Plex is running properly over the internet.\n\nAfterwards I tried seeing how VRChat would work after these changes. And surprisingly there were no random disconnects happening anymore since then (around 2 months now at the time of writing).\n\nLeaving all this info here in case anyone finds it valuable.\"",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-07-05T06:29:47.851Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "So this has been happening for some time now, but as of recent its been a lot more often. It happens at least once every time I am in VR and sometimes several more times whereas before it was something that would only happen rarely. I'm not sure if any changes were made to the real-time networking in VRChat, but either way these happen much more often than before. \n\nMost of the time they have no reason behind them, just completely random. I'd be talking to a friend face-to-face and then just randomly I'd get disconnected/not responding/timed out. \n\nAnd today (7/5/2024 at 08:00 UTC), it pretty much showed the issue full blast constantly.   (May have been an outage or something but nothing heard from the VRC team about it)\n\nAside from that though, I believe one of the reasons that VRChat decides to disconnect mainly is when the ISP IP lease is renewed for someone due to DHCP. It seems VRChat can't keep someone connected when they get a new lease. Maybe something can be done about this in the future?\n\nAs for everything else though, feels completely random no idea why it happens.",
